Fix filegroup circular deps in rules_distroless apt packages.

Debian has legitimate circular dependencies (e.g. libc6 <-> libgcc-s1).
The per-arch filegroup target includes both ":data" and deps on other
packages' filegroups, which creates a Bazel analysis cycle. Fix by:
1. Removing ":data" from the per-arch filegroup (it's already in the
   alias), and
2. Changing deps to point at ":data" targets instead of filegroups.

From https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_distroless/pull/164
(not yet merged upstream as of 2026-03-22).

--- a/apt/private/deb_translate_lock.bzl
+++ b/apt/private/deb_translate_lock.bzl
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@

 filegroup(
     name = "{target_name}",
-    srcs = select({deps}) + [":data"],
+    srcs = select({deps}),
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
 )
 '''
@@ -191,7 +191,7 @@
                 control_targets = '"@%s//:control"' % repo_name,
                 src = '"@%s//:data"' % repo_name,
                 deps = starlark_codegen_utils.to_list_attr([
-                    "//%s/%s" % (dep["name"], package["arch"])
+                    "//%s/%s:data" % (dep["name"], package["arch"])
                     for dep in package["dependencies"]
                 ]),
                 urls = package["urls"],
